    "description": "The ``filter`` extension is a built-in extension that provides an efficient way to filter, validate and sanitize data. Give it a string, and check that it satisfies a specific format.\n\n``filter`` works on incoming data, such as ``$_GET`` or ``$_POST``, but also on free variables.",
    "code": "<?php\n\n$data = [\n    'age' => '123 years',\n    'name'  => 'John Doe',\n];\n\n$filters = [\n    'age'   => FILTER_VALIDATE_INT,\n    'name'   => FILTER_SANITIZE_ENCODED,\n];\n\nprint_r(filter_var_array($data, $filters));\n\n?>",
